<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  Harbor Android TV. Permits cleartext HTTP to the on-device torrent engine,
  and to nothing else.

  WHY THIS FILE HAS TO EXIST

  Tauri 2.10.1 generates app/build.gradle.kts containing:

      defaultConfig {
          manifestPlaceholders["usesCleartextTraffic"] = "false"
      }
      buildTypes {
          getByName("debug") {
              manifestPlaceholders["usesCleartextTraffic"] = "true"
          }
          getByName("release") {
              // no override, so the "false" above stands
          }
      }

  (Verified by extracting the template from the CLI binary this repo has
  installed, not from documentation.)

  Harbor's torrent engine serves http://127.0.0.1:11470. So P2P playback is
  permitted under `tauri android dev` and forbidden in the shipped release APK.
  It fails in the WebView's network stack, so Rust logs nothing, the engine
  reports healthy, and video simply never starts. That is a
  works-in-dev-dead-in-release trap, which is the expensive kind.

  On API 24 and above a network security config overrides
  android:usesCleartextTraffic completely, so this file alone is the fix. There
  is no need to also flip the gradle placeholder, and flipping it instead of
  using this file would open cleartext app-wide.

  INSTALL

    1. copy to
         src-tauri/gen/android/app/src/main/res/xml/network_security_config.xml
    2. add this attribute to the <application> tag in
         src-tauri/gen/android/app/src/main/AndroidManifest.xml
         android:networkSecurityConfig="@xml/network_security_config"

  Both files live under gen/android, which Tauri generates once and which has
  no override hook, so they must be committed and hand maintained. That is a
  git decision for js.

  tauri.localhost is listed because that is the origin Tauri serves the app
  from on Android. Tauri intercepts those requests before the network stack, so
  it should not need the entry, but listing loopback costs nothing and removes
  a variable from the first on-device debugging session.
-->
<network-security-config>
    <base-config cleartextTrafficPermitted="false" />
    <domain-config cleartextTrafficPermitted="true">
        <domain includeSubdomains="false">127.0.0.1</domain>
        <domain includeSubdomains="false">localhost</domain>
        <domain includeSubdomains="false">tauri.localhost</domain>
    </domain-config>
</network-security-config>
